# Experimental deployment documentation. DO NOT enable before MTA acceptance.
# The opt-in LMTP runtime exists, but full mail delivery/bounce acceptance does
# not. Generate an explicit map generation with `listmngr aliases regen` first.
# See docs/POSTFIX_MAPS.md for limits, permissions and operator-owned activation.
#
# Dedicated relay-domain MTA example only; replace GENERATION with the exact
# generation-UUID printed by the CLI. Never overwrite a shared MTA's settings.
# List domains must not also be in mydestination or virtual domain classes.
# relay_domains = regexp:/var/lib/listmngr/postfix/GENERATION/domains.regexp
# transport_maps = regexp:/var/lib/listmngr/postfix/GENERATION/transport.regexp
# relay_recipient_maps = regexp:/var/lib/listmngr/postfix/GENERATION/recipients.regexp
# smtpd_reject_unlisted_recipient = yes
# smtpd_relay_restrictions = permit_mynetworks, reject_unauth_destination
# recipient_delimiter =
# lmtp_destination_recipient_limit = 1
#
# Example generated transport row:
# /^list@example\.org$/ lmtp:[127.0.0.1]:8024
#
# Activation gate:
#   postconf -m  # must include regexp; do NOT compile these as hash maps
#   postfix check
#   postmap -q example.org regexp:/var/lib/listmngr/postfix/GENERATION/domains.regexp
#   postmap -q list@example.org regexp:/var/lib/listmngr/postfix/GENERATION/recipients.regexp
# Also query unknown recipients and ensure NOT FOUND, not catch-all acceptance.
# Postmap lookup is not daemon delivery evidence. Reload only after separately
# authorized MTA end-to-end acceptance and after granting the MTA read access.
